Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

Diagnosis uses item embedding weights, sequence features, and positive/negative 
item scores. It calls `log2feats(sequence)` to obtain features for every 
sequence position, then `predict_score(features, items)` to score candidates. 
Model implementation is absent, so the encoder architecture and computation of 
the final user representation cannot be established. This probe evaluates 
features across valid positions rather than explicitly selecting the final 
position.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(model, device)` stores the supplied model or compatibility view 
and its `meta_data`, `review_data`, and `user_train`. The latter two are unused.
Under the adapter contract, the view exposes the actual trained module through 
`view.model` and must support the hooks used here, including evaluation mode.

The loader supplies `(None, sequence, positive, negative)` with tensors shaped 
`B × L`. Sequences pass through `log2feats`; stacked positive/negative IDs have 
shape `B × L × 2`. Positions with positive ID zero are excluded.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Embedding collapse:** Excludes padding embedding zero, samples up to 2,048 
items using seed 42, normalizes embeddings, and averages off-diagonal cosine 
similarities. Mapping through `(mean_cosine + 1)/2` yields the collapse score. 
Higher indicates directional alignment; roughly orthogonal embeddings score 
around 0.5.
- **Score separation:** In evaluation mode without gradients, processes up to 
ten loader batches and computes positive minus negative logits. Higher mean and 
10th-percentile margins indicate stronger separation. Lower negative-wins and 
small-margin rates indicate fewer ranking errors and weak separations; the 
small-margin threshold is 0.5.
- **Category breakdown:** Counts category occurrences separately for positive 
and negative items in weak-margin and wrong-rank cases, reporting up to twenty 
categories per group.

# Perturbation & Tests

No sequence perturbation, shuffling, or sensitivity test occurs. Sampling 
selects embeddings for inspection; loader negatives provide the ranking 
comparison.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

`run_full_diagnosis` returns `metrics` and `metric_definitions`. Metrics contain
the collapse score, four margin statistics, and nested category counts. 
`diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` embeds both dictionaries and requests JSON 
containing `status`, `core_findings`, `key_implications`, and `evidence`.

These probes measure training-sample geometry and separation, not validation 
HR@10, generalization, recommendation diversity, or simulator traits. Category 
metadata is unavailable in this task, so category lists remain empty. Missing 
valid positions produce zero statistics, potentially obscuring missing evidence.
Evaluation mode is not restored afterward.

