INFO:self_evolverec:The new idea for diagnosis in iteration 1:
{
  "description": "Implement a paired temporal diagnostic adapter that measures dependence on recent content, earlier order, and positional handling through the actual trained model, with explicit controls for padding artifacts and training memorization.",
  "motivation": "Qualitative feedback suggests broad associations sometimes outrank specific recent interests, while existing embedding and margin probes cannot distinguish content, order, recency, or implementation effects. At 0% progress, controlled measurements are a feasible foundation before training a recency residual scorer. Training-history diagnostics establish model dependence and fit; only unchanged host validation measures benchmark generalization, and repeated validation consultation remains exploratory.",
  "implementation_notes": "Preserve DiagnosisProbe(view, device), run_full_diagnosis(train_loader), and diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis). Use view.model as the actual nn.Module; enter eval mode under torch.inference_mode() and restore its previous training state in finally. Retain existing embedding and margin probes, but explicitly define mean cosine as directional alignment rather than proof of collapse. Category breakdowns must remain empty because category metadata is unavailable; do not use reviews, ratings, prices, stores, or simulator traits.\n\nUse log2feats and predict_score through an architecture-specific scoring adapter. Document left/right padding, positional indexing, attention masks, and readout. Baseline SASRec scores the final array position; choosing the last nonzero ID automatically is not a generally valid replacement. Causal masks do not exclude padded keys, and key padding masks do not zero padded query outputs. Verify the actual implementation rather than assuming padding embedding zero makes holes inert. Do not silently change trained inference behavior to repair a diagnostic. Any correction that changes the trained model requires a separate training change and synchronized predictor writer.\n\nA concrete bounded default is up to 50 eligible training users per dataset, sampled with a local seed-42 generator and sorted ID ordering. For each user select the final training event as target and use its preceding prefix, truncated to the model context length. Require at least five prefix events for matched removal controls and report excluded-user counts. These targets participated in optimization and therefore measure training fit. Never read validation or test labels through the probe. Earlier occurrences of the target remain in the prefix. Do not modify preprocessing or split membership.\n\nFor sampled diagnostics use the target once plus 99 unique uniform negatives, excluding padding, target, and original-prefix IDs; reuse the exact pool under every intervention. If fewer than 99 eligible negatives exist, report the example unavailable rather than sampling duplicates. A separate complete-training-history exclusion condition may be reported, keeping the target eligible even if repeated. Persist pools and exclusion-policy identifiers beneath the trial directory. These auxiliary pools are not substitutes for the host's pinned validation candidates. Use descending score then ascending item ID for diagnostic ties; preserve host tie handling for official metrics.\n\nSet removal count m=max(1,floor(0.2*(n-1))) among the n-1 prefix events preceding the final event. Compare the m most recent eligible events, m oldest events, and m uniformly sampled eligible events while retaining the final event. Use three deterministic repeats for random removal and shuffling; fixed interventions need one evaluation. Compare earlier-only shuffling with full shuffling. Test deletion of the final event separately and repack to the ordinary final query position. Log selected indices and effective intervention strength for reproduction.\n\nFor removal controls distinguish holes, packing with original position IDs retained, and ordinary reindexed packing. With correctly excluded padded keys, identical surviving position IDs, order, and readout, holes and preserved-position packing should closely agree within documented numerical tolerance. Check finite outputs and perturb padded-key representations to verify exclusion. If the architecture cannot expose position IDs or masks without changing its semantics, report that control unsupported; do not claim recency identification from unverified hole masking. Complement removal with fixed-position substitutions using actual same-dataset items: sample unseen donor items from the same training-frequency decile, using deterministic nearest-decile fallback. These substitutions avoid holes but remain potentially out of distribution and are not preference counterfactuals.\n\nReport original and perturbed target ranks, reciprocal ranks, sampled HR@10, rank differences, top-10 overlap defined as intersection size divided by ten, sample counts, and explicit metric definitions. Keep sampled overlap distinct from full-catalog overlap. Average repeats within user; bootstrap users independently within each dataset using 1,000 seed-42 replicates while carrying all paired outcomes together. Compute each replicate's equally weighted four-dataset macro difference and percentile 95% interval. If any category has no eligible examples, report the four-category macro statistic unavailable rather than silently averaging fewer categories. Intervals condition on fixed trained models and candidate pools; they exclude training-seed uncertainty and repeated-selection bias.\n\nInclude inexpensive descriptive controls: last-item dot-product scoring using learned item embeddings; a transition baseline fitted only from adjacent training interactions with add-one smoothing and frequency-weighted aggregation over the prefix; and mean normalized history-embedding similarity. These controls identify plausible shortcuts but are themselves fitted on training data and are not proof of useful generalization. Stratify descriptively by history length and repeated-item fraction; do not equate repeated IDs with semantic purpose.\n\nBefore further comparisons, freeze diagnostic definitions and the checkpoint schedule. Across all logged checkpoints and trials, report exploratory Spearman correlation between predeclared diagnostic quantities and official macro validation HR@10, adjacent-checkpoint improvement-direction agreement with ties reported separately, and category consistency. Correlated checkpoints are not independent replications; missing outcomes remain missing. If the host does not expose paired per-user validation outcomes, report only its available aggregate results and omit validation bootstrap intervals. Never reconstruct or alter the evaluator. Winner intervals do not correct repeated-selection optimism; independent confirmation awaits the host's final evaluation.\n\nFor the twenty required simulator users, preserve five users per dataset and full-catalog unseen-item scoring. Encode each history once per perturbation, score catalog chunks, mask padding and complete training histories, and merge chunk-local top-k results with deterministic tie handling. Cache item representations only while weights remain fixed; key all caches by checkpoint, dataset, history, perturbation, and exclusion policy. Preallocate at most 600 GPU-seconds for this initial diagnostic phase within the shared 43,200-second budget, reserving required simulator scoring before optional controls. Log elapsed time and omissions; do not replace required full-catalog recommendations with sampled candidates.\n\nPreserve DATA_DIR=os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], all four dataset routes, preprocessing seed 0, training seed 42, single-GPU execution, and the existing SASREC_EPOCHS environment default of 200. Write all artifacts beneath the trial directory. No extra datasets or pretrained weights are required. Subsequent architecture changes must update training and the predictor writer together.",
  "pseudocode": "class DiagnosisProbe:\n    def __init__(self, view, device):\n        self.view, self.device = view, device\n\n    def run_full_diagnosis(self, train_loader):\n        previous_mode = self.view.model.training\n        try:\n            self.view.model.eval()\n            with torch.inference_mode():\n                checks = inspect_scoring_contract_and_check_padding(self.view)\n                original_metrics = measure_existing_probes(train_loader)\n                examples = deterministic_training_prefix_targets(seed=42, max_users_per_dataset=50)\n                records = []\n                for example in examples:\n                    candidates = fixed_unique_candidates(example, seed=42)\n                    if candidates is None:\n                        record_unavailable(example, 'insufficient eligible candidates')\n                        continue\n                    baseline = score_actual_model(example.prefix, candidates, checks.readout)\n                    for intervention in predeclared_interventions(example, checks):\n                        if not intervention.supported:\n                            record_unavailable(example, intervention.reason)\n                            continue\n                        changed = score_actual_model(intervention.sequence, candidates,\n                                                     intervention.readout,\n                                                     intervention.position_ids)\n                        assert_all_finite(baseline, changed)\n                        records.append(paired_rank_hit_and_overlap(baseline, changed,\n                                                                  tie_rule='score_desc_item_id_asc'))\n                metrics = merge(original_metrics, checks.metrics,\n                                bootstrap_category_macro(average_repeats_per_user(records),\n                                                         replicates=1000, seed=42))\n                return {'metrics': metrics,\n                        'metric_definitions': explicit_definitions_with_scope_and_missingness(metrics)}\n        finally:\n            self.view.model.train(previous_mode)\n\ndef diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis):\n    return render_prompt(raw_diagnosis['metrics'],\n                         raw_diagnosis['metric_definitions'],\n                         instruction='Use measured evidence only. Separate training fit, intervention dependence, implementation artifacts, and official validation accuracy. Treat missing controls as unavailable. Do not infer causal preferences, ownership satisfaction, compatibility without specifications, or unobserved simulator traits.')",
  "originality": {
    "score": 5,
