  "implementation_notes": "Preserve all four dataset routes, preprocessing seed 0, training seed 42, evaluation seed 42, DATA_DIR = os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], baseline loss/optimizer/batching, and the SASREC_EPOCHS environment default of 200. Keep execution single-GPU and artifacts beneath each trial directory. No new datasets or pretrained weights are needed.\n\nFor each prefix, use x_t = sqrt(d) * item_emb(sequence_t), validity mask m_t, fixed rho = exp(-1/5), u_t = rho*u_(t-1) + m_t*x_t, and z_t = rho*z_(t-1) + m_t. Set r_t = u_t/clamp(z_t, eps), apply parameter-free F.layer_norm(r_t, (d,), weight=None, bias=None), and explicitly zero padded fused outputs. Set gamma = sigmoid(alpha), initializing alpha = log(0.05/0.95). Keep decay fixed in the selected experiment; learning decay is a later hypothesis outside this search. Multiply fused features by unscaled candidate embeddings, matching baseline target scaling. The recurrence costs O(BLd) work, O(Bd) running state, and O(BLd) retained prefix/autograd memory; a Python loop adds L sequential launches while SASRec attention cost remains unchanged.\n\nMake log2feats(sequence) return fused B x L x d features everywhere. Define predict_score explicitly: aligned item IDs B x L produce B x L scores; aligned candidate IDs B x L x K produce B x L x K scores; final features B x d with shared candidates K or per-user candidates B x K produce B x K scores. Use explicit shape checks and operations rather than ambiguous broadcasting. For nonempty left-padded inference inputs, use the final fused feature at index -1. Save the gain, decay horizon, architecture identifier, and baseline configuration; update the predictor writer to reconstruct and load the identical trained architecture.\n\nPredeclare eight configurations, each covering all four datasets: (1) the exact baseline with a residual bypass, (2) baseline with positive trainable global logit scale initialized to 1, (3) uniform-history residual with fixed gain 0.05, (4) last-item residual with fixed gain 0.05, (5) fixed-gain geometric residual with gain 0.05, (6) selected learned-gain geometric residual, (7) configuration 6 with both history-side and candidate-side residual embeddings detached while keeping the backbone gradients and gain trainable, and (8) configuration 6 with timestamp decay. Normalize pooling outputs identically. For configuration 8, use prefix-available elapsed times and a fixed dataset horizon of five times the median strictly positive adjacent training-history gap, calculated from training interactions only. If timestamps cannot support this definition, mark this configuration unavailable without adding a substitute. Timestamp recurrence uses elapsed time between valid events and leaves padding state unchanged.\n\nMatch shared-parameter initialization, minibatches, negative samples, optimizer, and training duration across configurations. Fix checkpoint evaluation at every completed epoch, select by the host-compatible four-category macro validation HR@10, and resolve checkpoint ties by earliest epoch and configuration ties by the listed order. Plan runs using measured runtime and stop before exceeding the shared 43,200 GPU-second cap, including diagnostics, debugging, and failed trials. Report unfinished configurations explicitly; do not expand the grid. A gate-disabled inference pass on a residual-trained checkpoint measures branch dependence, but cannot replace training the exact baseline bypass. Inference-only positive scaling cannot change ranks; training-time scaling can change optimization.\n\nRetain DiagnosisProbe(view, device), run_full_diagnosis(train_loader), and diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis). Use view.model as the trained module; save its prior training flag, call eval(), use no_grad(), and restore the flag in a finally block. Return metrics and metric_definitions, including sample counts, thresholds, perturbation settings, and null values for unavailable measurements. Preserve existing embedding geometry and margin statistics, explicitly stating that these measure fitted behavior. Category metadata is unavailable, so retain empty category lists with an availability flag rather than inferred categories. Never use unavailable ratings, review text, prices, stores, or unobserved diversity/conformity traits.\n\nFor additional diagnostics, take each eligible training user's final training event as a fixed diagnostic target and restrict input to preceding events. Label this as fitted-model reliance because the target participated in fitting. Use diagnostic seed 42 to draw 99 unique negatives from the dataset catalog, excluding the target and the user's original training history; freeze candidates, exclusions, and deterministic tie-breaking across every intervention. These candidate sets are separate from pinned host validation candidates. Do not resplit the benchmark or claim that removing the target from probe input removes training influence. Any generalization claim must rely on targets excluded from fitting; the pinned validation remains the available selection evidence and is subject to repeated-selection optimism. Global temporal leakage cannot be repaired by a diagnostic intervention without changing the benchmark split [6].\n\nUse the same eligible users with at least six prefix events. Delete k = min(3, floor(prefix_length/2)) most recent events, explicitly including the final event, versus k oldest events and k uniformly sampled events. Report position-preserving evidence removal separately from compaction. For position-preserving removal, retain original positions and the original prediction-query slot while removing deleted item evidence from attention keys/values; do not substitute an untrained mask token. Verify that the actual encoder permits the required query and attention masks; otherwise report this intervention unavailable. Compaction repacks surviving events using the normal left-padding path and therefore changes adjacency and positional distances. For shuffling, permute only earlier valid events, retaining the last item, item multiset, length, and padding. Use five seeded permutations and aggregate repetitions within each user.\n\nReport paired target-rank changes, diagnostic HR@10 changes, top-10 overlap, eligibility counts, and results by dataset, history length, and target training-popularity bin. Bootstrap users within each category with 2,000 seed-42 replicates, preserving paired conditions and equal-weight category macro-averaging. Aggregate perturbation repetitions before resampling. These 95% percentile intervals quantify uncertainty conditional on fitted models and fixed candidates; they do not capture training-seed variability, remove target contamination, establish causal preferences, or correct validation-selection optimism. Keep twenty-user full-catalog feedback as qualitative evidence rather than population evaluation. Report title/description availability and abstain from compatibility or need claims without explicit evidence; potential repeated-title redundancy is not proof of unwanted ownership.\n\nVerify recurrence outputs and gradients against explicit causal geometric sums; verify padding invariance, causal independence, and consistent training/diagnostic/inference logits in evaluation mode. Confirm checkpoint round-trip parity and exact disabled-control baseline scores and gradients. These checks establish implementation consistency, not benchmark improvement. No performance gain is claimed before execution.",
  "pseudocode": "Predeclare the eight configurations and the shared search-budget cap.\nFor each affordable complete configuration:\n  For each of the four datasets:\n    initialize the shared SASRec parameters with training seed 42\n    initialize alpha = log(0.05 / 0.95) when the gain is learned\n    for each baseline training batch:\n      H = baseline_SASRec_features(sequence)\n      u, z = zeros(B, d), zeros(B, 1)\n      for t in causal sequence order:\n        m = sequence[:, t] != 0\n        x = sqrt(d) * item_emb(sequence[:, t])\n        u = rho * u + m[:, None] * x\n        z = rho * z + m[:, None]\n        r = parameter_free_layer_norm(u / clamp_min(z, eps))\n        F[:, t] = m[:, None] * (H[:, t] + sigmoid(alpha) * r)\n      positive_scores = dot_aligned(F, unscaled_item_emb(positive))\n      negative_scores = dot_aligned(F, unscaled_item_emb(negative))\n      optimize the unchanged baseline loss on valid target positions\n    evaluate checkpoints under the pinned validation protocol\n    save model, architecture settings, decay, gain, and matching predictor writer\nSelect only by equal-weight four-category validation HR@10, with declared tie-breaking.\nFreeze selected models and run fixed-candidate paired perturbation diagnostics.\nReport fitted reliance separately from validation selection and full-catalog qualitative feedback.\nStop before the shared GPU-second cap; do not add configurations.",
