      - Analysis: {"status":"NEEDS_IMPROVEMENT","core_findings":["Training margins are positive on average, but negatives outrank positives in 17.4–24.0% of sampled training pairs; Industrial_and_Scientific has the weakest separation.","Deleting the final context item reduces training-target HR@10 by 6–16 percentage points across datasets. This indicates intervention sensitivity, but unsupported position and padding controls prevent attributing it specifically to recency."],"key_implications":["Positive average margins coexist with substantial training-pair ranking errors.","Embedding alignment scores near 0.5 indicate near-zero mean cosine, providing no evidence of directional collapse or recommendation diversity.","These training-based diagnostics do not establish generalization; official validation accuracy is unavailable."],"evidence":{"headline_metrics":{"training_negative_beats_positive_rate_range":[0.174,0.24],"Industrial_and_Scientific:pos_neg_margin_mean":1.1163,"Industrial_and_Scientific:pos_neg_margin_p10":-0.7694,"delete_final_training_hr10_drop_range":[0.06,0.16],"embedding_collapse_score_range":[0.5028,0.5068]},"brief_metric_read":{"training_negative_beats_positive_rate_range":"Fraction of sampled valid training pairs with negative margin.","delete_final_training_hr10_drop_range":"Absolute declines on training targets; position and padding effects remain unresolved.","embedding_collapse_score_range":"Transformed directional alignment, not proof of collapse."}}}
    
