INFO:self_evolverec:The new idea for model in iteration 2:
{
  "description": "Add a baseline-preserving gated recent-prefix residual to SASRec and train with 32 uniform negatives using generalized BCE at t=0.75. Share encoder parameters between full and independently encoded five-item prefixes, retaining independent models and dataset routing for all four categories.",
  "motivation": "The user diagnosis identifies stale interests and broadly related recommendations crowding out specific current preferences. A recent-prefix branch supplies explicit local evidence while preserving full-history preferences, addressing those two user-facing failures. Electronics’ 14.95% sampled wrong-rank rate motivates stronger discrimination. These are hypotheses requiring pinned validation; training margins cannot establish HR@10 gains, compatibility, or purchase satisfaction.",
  "implementation_notes": "Preserve DATA_DIR = os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], preprocessing seed 0, training seed 42, unchanged splits, four-category routing, and SASREC_EPOCHS default 200. Write all artifacts beneath the trial directory. Use only available histories, titles, descriptions, and timestamps; this proposal requires histories alone. Do not consume the unavailable ratings, review text, categories, prices, stores, or simulator traits.\n\nFor every valid next-item training position, construct a recent window from its causal prefix, never including its target or subsequent interactions. Left-pad item IDs by four and unfold with width five and stride one to obtain B x L x 5 windows. Select valid positions and encode windows independently with the shared SASRec encoder. Use fixed right-aligned positional slots 0 through 4 at both training and inference; padding remains masked. Retain each window’s final state. This is not interchangeable with sliding-window attention across layers. Materialize embeddings only after chunking windows. Handle padded query rows safely: permit their self-attention entry and zero their outputs, while blocking padded keys for valid queries. Respect the opposite boolean-mask conventions of TransformerEncoder and SDPA.\n\nLet h be the original full-prefix feature and r the recent feature. Define g = sigmoid(Linear(concat(h, r, log1p(prefix_length)))) and h_new = h + a*g*r, with a a learned scalar initialized exactly to zero, gate weights zero, and gate bias -2. Add no output LayerNorm or projection. Use unchanged item dot products for scores. Check initial score equivalence in eval mode against the same baseline checkpoint. The recent branch receives gradients after a departs zero. Its lack of guaranteed norm control is a limitation; track feature norms rather than introducing an untested normalization change.\n\nLet N count nonpadding items. Draw k=32 negatives independently with replacement from all N items except the current target; duplicates count as separate draws. Set alpha=k/(N-1), beta=1-t+t*alpha, t=0.75, and compute each valid position’s loss as (beta*softplus(-positive_logit) + sum(softplus(negative_logits)))/(k+1). Average over valid positions. Compute softplus in float32 or higher. Do not average positive and negative terms separately. The positive-logit transformation is unnecessary with this equivalent direct objective; inference always uses original dot-product scores. Report that k=32 is a budget-conscious proposal, while the cited authors recommend k=256. Do not claim full-catalog calibration after excluding all known positives; such exclusion changes sampling support. Target-only exclusion preserves the theorem’s support but leaves observed and unobserved false negatives possible.\n\nIndependent recent encoding repeats projection and feedforward computation. Profile complete optimizer steps, validation, and diagnosis before committing to the ablation schedule. To bound window activations while preserving full-branch gradients, encode the full sequence once, create a detached feature proxy requiring gradients, backpropagate globally normalized chunk losses into that proxy and shared parameters, then backpropagate the accumulated proxy gradient through the original full encoder graph. Step the optimizer once after all chunks. Compare its gradients against an unchunked tiny batch with dropout disabled. This validation is necessary because simply retaining every chunk loss until one backward defeats the intended memory bound.\n\nPredeclare four primary ablations: unchanged single-negative BCE baseline; unchanged architecture with multi-negative gBCE; recent residual with baseline loss; combined model. Add a gated full-history residual control, replacing r with h while matching gate, normalization placement, and training settings, before claiming a specifically temporal mechanism. All retain the baseline optimizer and other hyperparameters initially. Allocate equal aggregate GPU-time ceilings after profiling; count training, validation, diagnosis, debugging, and failures toward 43,200 GPU-seconds across all four categories and configurations. Fix checkpoint cadence and choose the highest macro validation HR@10, breaking exact ties in favor of the earlier checkpoint and then the simpler configuration. Log every evaluated setting and consumed GPU time. Keep seeds fixed; bootstrap uncertainty does not replace training-seed replication.\n\nIf the unchanged evaluator exposes paired per-user hit indicators, bootstrap 10,000 paired resamples with a separate analysis RNG seeded 42, independently sampling 200 users with replacement within each category and averaging category differences equally. Report percentile 95% intervals, category results, and discordant wins/losses. Do not change the evaluator to obtain unavailable outputs. These intervals condition on fixed candidates and training seed; they neither remove winner-selection bias nor establish full-catalog performance.\n\nUpdate the predictor writer and working/predict.py with the exact fused architecture, learned scalar, gate state, right-aligned positions, window size, and category checkpoints. Preserve DiagnosisProbe(view, device), run_full_diagnosis(train_loader), and diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis). view.model must remain the actual trained nn.Module; item_emb, log2feats, and predict_score must expose the fused scoring path. Preserve user_train, meta_data, and review_data compatibility attributes without inventing unavailable fields. Return measured metrics and definitions; mark unavailable probes explicitly and do not infer categories from empty breakdowns. Compute diagnostic item alignment excluding padding, using identical sampling across compared models. Record margin diagnostics, residual magnitude, gate distribution, and feature norms as explanatory measures, never replacement selection metrics. Twenty real training users, five per category, must still receive full-catalog unseen-item recommendations for the native simulator.",
  "pseudocode": "predeclare_configurations_budget_checkpoint_cadence_and_tie_breaks()\nfor configuration in declared_configurations:\n    for category in FOUR_DATASETS:\n        initialize_baseline_SASRec_and_optional_residual(seed=42)\n        # Keep preprocessing seed 0 and original optimizer/settings.\n        for batch in unchanged_training_loader:\n            optimizer.zero_grad()\n            full = model.original_log2feats(batch.sequence)\n            if residual_enabled:\n                proxy = full.detach().requires_grad_(True)\n                windows = left_pad(batch.sequence, 4).unfold(1, 5, 1)\n            else:\n                proxy = full\n            valid_count = count(batch.positive != 0)\n            for chunk in valid_position_chunks:\n                h = select(proxy, chunk)\n                if residual_enabled:\n                    r = shared_encoder(windows[chunk], positions=right_aligned_slots_0_to_4).last_state\n                    g = sigmoid(gate(concat(h, r, log1p(prefix_lengths[chunk]))))\n                    h = h + zero_initialized_learned_scalar * g * r\n                negatives = draw_with_replacement_excluding_target_and_padding(k=32)\n                positive_logits = dot(h, item_emb(batch.positive[chunk]))\n                negative_logits = dot(h, item_emb(negatives))\n                beta = 1 - 0.75 + 0.75 * 32 / (nonpadding_catalog_size - 1)\n                position_loss = (beta * softplus(-positive_logits) + sum(softplus(negative_logits), dim=-1)) / 33\n                backward(sum(position_loss) / valid_count)\n                # Baseline-loss ablations instead use the unchanged single-negative BCE.\n            if residual_enabled:\n                full.backward(proxy.grad)\n            optimizer.step()\n            enforce_shared_aggregate_GPU_budget()\n        save_checkpoints_and_matching_predictor_under_trial_directory()\nselect_using_only_pinned_four_category_macro_validation_HR_at_10()\nreport_category_results_cost_and_available_paired_uncertainty()\nrun_compatible_measured_diagnostics_and_native_training_user_recommendations()",
  "originality": {
    "score": 3,
    "positive": "The combination is explicitly tied to the supplied temporal and discrimination failures and includes controls testing its proposed mechanism.",
    "negative": "Recent-history encoders, gates, residual initialization, and multi-negative objectives are established techniques; their combination is incremental."
  },
  "future_potential": {
