      - Analysis: {"status":"NEEDS_IMPROVEMENT","core_findings":["Electronics shows weaker in-sample separation: 9.61% of fixed positive-minus-negative margins are negative, versus 0–0.47% elsewhere. This is a relative weakness, not a calibrated failure threshold.","All four models are more sensitive to deleting newest interactions than oldest interactions. Keeping the latest interaction during shuffling reduces, but does not eliminate, measured sensitivity.","Each category covers 1,280 sampled training users. Position-preserving deletion and position-only controls are unsupported (null; 0 eligible users); dataset fields and inapplicable swap measurements are also null."],"key_implications":["Recent history contributes substantially to measured scores, but deletion also changes context and absolute positions, preventing a causal recency interpretation.","Embedding mean cosines of 0.078–0.228 do not establish collapse or recommendation diversity; these single-checkpoint measurements do not establish training dynamics.","These sampled in-sample, two-candidate statistics establish neither HR@10 nor empirical gains; selection remains independently measured macro validation HR@10."],"evidence":{"headline_metrics":{"Electronics_negative_margin_fraction":0.09609375,"Electronics_margin_p10":0.053857579827308655,"Movies_and_TV_delete_newest_margin_delta":-5.9113446360453965,"Movies_and_TV_delete_oldest_margin_delta":-0.04862250741571188,"Electronics_shuffle_ordering_flip":0.11109375,"Electronics_shuffle_keep_latest_ordering_flip":0.06203125},"brief_metric_read":{"negative_margin_fraction":"Positive scores below one fixed uniform history-excluded negative.","margin_delta":"Perturbed minus intact margin for identical candidates.","ordering_flip":"Frequency with which margin>0 changes truth value; not a top-10 ranking metric."}}}
    
