INFO:self_evolverec:The new idea for model in iteration 3:
{
  "description": "Add a causal recent-history residual to each per-dataset SASRec model and train candidate cross-entropy with 32 unique uniform negatives. At every valid position, exponentially pool the last five observed item embeddings, apply a learned directed projection and a prefix-dependent scalar gate, and multiply the residual by a zero-initialized learned scalar. Treat this as a modest combination of established mechanisms, tested through a four-variant factorial comparison.",
  "motivation": "The proposal explicitly targets two user-facing failures: older interests overpowering recent activity, and broad historical similarity admitting items without a specific current task or content connection. Recent conditioning addresses the former; projected recent-to-target associations provide a testable mechanism for the latter, without establishing actual usefulness. Candidate competition targets the model-facing Electronics weakness: 8.42% negative-win rate, 0.210 tenth-percentile margin, and 12.47% margins below 0.5 on observed neural training pairs. These associations do not establish causal explanations, validation gains, compatibility, complementarity, immediate demand, or dislike. Electronics embedding alignment of approximately 0.677 is a descriptive diagnostic, not evidence of poor recommendation diversity.",
  "implementation_notes": "Preserve Movies_and_TV, Industrial_and_Scientific, Electronics, and CDs_and_Vinyl, their dataset routing, unchanged benchmark splits, preprocessing seed 0, training seed 42, DATA_DIR=os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], trial-local artifacts, and int(os.environ.get('SASREC_EPOCHS', '200')). Do not access hidden test labels, fetch data or pretrained weights, or modify the evaluator. Only histories, timestamps, titles and descriptions are available; ignore the contradictory generic metadata example listing unavailable ratings, reviews, categories, prices and stores.\n\nUse the original SASRec backbone, optimizer, batching and learning-rate schedule unchanged across the initial four variants. Before execution, serialize the inherited concrete settings and all new settings into each trial configuration. Define recent weights as exp(-j), where j=0 denotes the current observed item, over at most five nonpadding observations. Normalize over valid observations; return zero for an empty prefix. The source item at position t is observed and may enter its own next-item prediction; the target at t+1 must never enter the prefix. Set W to a normally initialized bias-free d-by-d linear map. Set G to a scalar affine map of concat(h,r,h-r), initialize its bias to zero and weights with a standard small random initialization, and set scalar a=0. Use z=h+tanh(a)*sigmoid(G(...))*W(r). With a=0, z=h and gradients into W and G through the residual are zero; a generally receives a gradient immediately. Do not also zero W. Monitor a, effective gate magnitude, residual-to-backbone norm ratio, and gradient norms. Identity initialization of this addition does not establish whole-model dynamical isometry.\n\nImplement extra negative sampling inside the existing user-aware sampler before user IDs are discarded. Preserve downstream batches (None, sequence, positive, negative), each tensor B x L; preserve the original negative tensor and expose additional sampled negatives through a separately indexed training-side payload synchronized with the batch, or use a training-only collate wrapper that consumes user IDs internally before yielding the required batch. Do not infer user identity from truncated histories. Sample 32 unique items uniformly without replacement from IDs 1..N excluding the target and the user's complete training-history set. Never inspect held-out interactions for exclusions. For fewer than 32 eligible items, sample all eligible items and mask remaining slots; skip CE positions with no eligible alternatives and count them. Vectorize rejection sampling and use an explicit eligible-pool fallback for dense users. Record pool sizes M and actual counts k; conditional inclusion probability is k/M. For the CE-only and combined variants, use the identical sampler algorithm and seeded streams, while recognizing that training trajectories differ. False negatives remain possible.\n\nUse unnormalized dot-product logits and temperature tau=1 initially. Optimize the mean valid-position CE over the positive and its sampled alternatives. This is a 33-candidate discrimination objective, not an unbiased full-softmax likelihood. Do not silently multiply by M/32 or add importance corrections: those define another objective, and even a partition estimate followed by a logarithm remains biased at finite sample size. Exclusions change support. Keep the baseline's original BCE and negative count in the baseline and residual-only cells, and label their comparison with CE as a combined objective-and-negative-count intervention. An equal-32-negative BCE/gBCE/CE comparison would isolate objectives, but is a deferred experiment requiring budget. gBCE uses independent sigmoid terms with its published beta correction, not temperature scaling; log its sampling assumptions and normalization if implemented.\n\nPredeclare baseline, CE-only, residual-only, and combined variants. Each receives at most 10,800 charged GPU-seconds across all four categories, training, diagnostics, validation, debugging and failures; all trials together remain within 43,200 GPU-seconds. Use one GPU per trial; concurrent slots do not increase the total budget. Keep the 200-epoch environment default. Evaluate every 10 completed epochs, use no early-stopping patience in this initial comparison, and stop at the shared epoch limit or variant budget cap. Reserve time within each cap for validation and required diagnostics. A macro checkpoint consists of four category checkpoints at the same evaluation milestone; select the largest measured pinned macro validation HR@10, breaking ties by earliest milestone. Record the actual category epochs and steps, and report incomplete milestones or budget truncation rather than inventing scores. Use the same pinned 200 validation users/category, 99 unique negatives, and evaluation seed 42 for every variant. Never substitute a local evaluator for the host's pinned selection metric.\n\nSave each validation user's binary hit with category and stable user identifier when the evaluator exposes it; otherwise mark paired inference unavailable rather than fabricate hits or change the evaluator. Using available hits, estimate pairwise macro differences with 10,000 category-stratified paired bootstrap replicates, seed 42, resampling 200 users independently within each category with shared indices across variants. Report percentile 95% intervals and discordant win/loss counts. Intervals condition on checkpoint selection, seed and candidate sets, excluding selection optimism and training variability. If significance is claimed across multiple comparisons, use separately valid paired tests with a declared multiplicity correction such as Holm; bootstrap intervals alone are not adjusted significance tests. Limit conclusions to the pinned sampled-candidate metric, which may disagree with full-catalog ranking. Record per-category and macro HR@10, checkpoint epoch/step, hardware, training/evaluation/diagnostic time, charged GPU-seconds and wall time.\n\nSerialize architecture settings, source/output embedding conventions, pooling decay, gate, projection, scalar, weights and category routing. Update the predictor writer so working/predict.py constructs the exact trained architecture. Reuse fused features and identical dot-product scoring in training and inference. Produce the native full-catalog unseen-item recommendations for twenty real training users, five/category, without inferring unobserved simulator traits. This candidate-independent branch needs no candidate-specific history attention; chunk catalog matrix multiplication if necessary.\n\nRetain DiagnosisProbe(view, device), run_full_diagnosis(train_loader), and diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis), returning measured metrics and definitions. view.model must be the actual trained nn.Module; preserve item_emb, user_train, meta_data and review_data accessors. Expose fused deployed features through log2feats and their matching dot-product scores through predict_score. Label changed neural-margin semantics explicitly: fused margins are not the previous backbone-only margins. If there is a separate deployed scoring wrapper, probe it directly; otherwise state that neural and deployed scores coincide. Report finite observation counts, exclusions, unique sampled items and sampled embedding counts; keep unavailable category breakdowns unavailable. Null deployed metrics in the supplied diagnosis are missing evidence, not zero error. The interpreter prompt must use actual measured values and definitions and avoid causal or user-trait claims.\n\nDo not expand the initial search to all suggested controls. If budget remains, prioritize last-item versus uniform-last-five versus exponential-last-five pooling, then a scale-matched global scalar versus learned gate or identity versus learned W. A global fixed coefficient must be tuned under the same budget to avoid attributing a scale benefit to adaptive gating. Symmetric W and separate source/target factors can probe directionality, but are deferred. Broader window, decay, temperature, loss and gate sweeps risk validation overfitting on only 800 users. Log every attempted configuration and failure; simulator feedback supplies hypotheses, never training preference labels. No improvement is claimed before measurement.",
  "pseudocode": "Predeclare four variants: original SASRec; CE-only; residual-only; residual+CE.\nFreeze common preprocessing/training seeds, backbone settings, validation cadence and budget policy.\nFor each variant, cap all four categories and diagnostics at 10,800 charged GPU-seconds:\n    For each unchanged category dataset:\n        Initialize SASRec; for residual variants initialize W normally, gate G, and a=0.\n        In the user-aware sampler, retain complete training-positive exclusion sets.\n        Generate required tensor batches; prepare additional negatives before discarding user IDs.\n        For every valid causal training position t:\n            h_t = SASRec(sequence)[t]\n            If residual enabled:\n                recent = last at most five observed nonpadding embeddings through t\n                r_t = sum_j exp(-j)*recent[j] / sum_j exp(-j)\n                g_t = sigmoid(G(concat(h_t, r_t, h_t-r_t)))\n                z_t = h_t + tanh(a)*g_t*W(r_t)\n            Else: z_t = h_t\n            If CE enabled:\n                eligible = catalog minus padding, target, complete known training positives\n                negatives = uniform_without_replacement(eligible, min(32, len(eligible)))\n                If no negatives: count exclusion and skip this CE position\n                logits = dot(z_t, output_item_embeddings([target] + negatives))\n                loss_t = cross_entropy(logits, target_index=0), tau=1\n            Else:\n                loss_t = original masked SASRec BCE using its original negative count\n        Optimize mean valid-position loss with unchanged baseline optimizer settings.\n        Save exact architecture configuration, model weights and training accounting.\n    At each common completed 10-epoch milestone within the budget:\n        Obtain pinned validation hits and four-category macro HR@10.\n        Save the four-model checkpoint bundle.\n    Select best complete macro checkpoint bundle; earliest milestone wins ties.\n    Generate working/predict.py using matching fused features, dot-product scoring and routing.\n    Run compatible diagnostics on actual trained models and record counts and definitions.\n    Generate full-catalog unseen-item recommendations for five training users/category.\nCompare variants using measured macro HR@10, category results and charged GPU time.\nWhere paired hits are available, compute stratified paired bootstrap intervals and discordant counts.\nReport missing evaluations explicitly; never infer hidden test performance.",
  "originality": {
