Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)
The model implementation is not supplied. Diagnosis accesses the trained module 
through `view.model` and nonpadding item embeddings through 
`view.item_emb.weight[1:]`. It obtains causal sequence representations from 
`view.log2feats(sequence)`, which must return **B × L × D** features. Each 
position predicts its next positive item; the probe does not specifically select
the final sequence representation.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks
`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` receives model hooks, training histories, 
metadata and review-data handles. Histories and metadata are retained but unused
by these probes; reviews are unavailable. `run_full_diagnosis(train_loader)` 
examines at most ten batches shaped `(None, sequence, positive, negative)`, with
B × L tensors.

Neural scores come from `view.predict_score(features, items)`. An optional 
deployed scorer is resolved from `view.score`, then `model.score`, and called 
with `(features, items, sequence)`. Both must produce B × L × 2 
positive/negative scores.

# Probes & Metrics
- **Embedding collapse score:** Samples up to 2,048 nonpadding embeddings using 
a local seed-42 generator. After excluding zero/nonfinite vectors, it computes 
mean off-diagonal cosine and maps it to [0,1]. Around 0.5 indicates isotropy; 
values toward 1 indicate directional alignment, potentially collapse. This does 
not establish recommendation quality.
- **Positive–negative margins:** At nonpadding positions with finite scores, 
computes positive minus negative. Reports mean, nearest-rank 10th percentile, 
negative-win rate, margin-below-0.5 rate and exact-tie rate. Larger positive 
margins and fewer negative wins generally indicate stronger training-pair 
separation; magnitudes and the threshold depend on score scale.
- **Deployed margins:** Reports the same statistics for the optional shared 
scorer, including its configured normalization or corrections. Raw and deployed 
magnitudes are not directly comparable.

# Perturbation & Tests
No sequences are perturbed and no sensitivity tests run. Scoring temporarily 
uses evaluation mode. Submodule modes and Python, NumPy, Torch CPU and 
selected-device CUDA RNG states are restored; loader-owned generators and worker
state are not rewound.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations
The result contains `metrics`, `metric_definitions`, `observation_counts` and 
`measurement_context`. Counts expose usable observations and nonfinite 
exclusions; null means unavailable evidence. Category breakdown is null because 
item categories are unavailable.

`diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` packages these measurements and caveats into 
instructions for a concise JSON interpretation. Probes do not measure 
candidate-set ranking, validation HR@10, recommendation diversity, user 
conformity or perturbation robustness. Model selection remains external 
four-category macro validation HR@10.

