Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)
The probe uses the trained `view.model` and nonpadding `view.item_emb` weights. 
Architecture internals are not supplied. `view.log2feats` computes 
representations from left-padded, right-aligned histories truncated to `maxlen`.
For B×L×D features, diagnosis selects the final slot; B×D features require the 
explicit `final_BD` contract. `view.predict_score` scores the fixed target and 
negative.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks
`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` reads public training histories and optional 
timestamps through `view.user_train`. It never consumes `train_loader`. A 
fingerprinted, persisted panel selects at most 1,280 eligible users using seed 
42. Each example predicts the final training interaction from its preceding 
prefix, paired with one fixed uniform negative excluded from the complete 
training history.

Diagnosis runs in evaluation mode without gradients. It restores module modes, 
random-generator states and registered buffers; detected buffer mutation raises 
an error.

# Probes & Metrics
- **Embedding alignment:** Mean pairwise cosine among up to 2,048 sampled 
nonzero item embeddings; mapped alignment is `(cosine+1)/2`. Higher values 
indicate greater average directional alignment, without establishing collapse or
diversity.
- **Intact discrimination:** Positive-minus-negative margin, fractions below 
zero and 0.5, exact ties, and margin p10. Positive margins favor the target; the
0.5 threshold is descriptive.
- **Perturbation response:** Margin change, ordering flips, perturbed ties and 
final-feature cosine distance measure score and representation sensitivity. 
Larger changes are not inherently better.
- **Intervention strength:** Changed-ID fraction, feasible partner counts and 
nonself-swap rates describe how much shuffling actually occurred.

# Perturbation & Tests
Seven conditions delete roughly 25% of newest, oldest or random prefix 
positions; shuffle all items or preserve the latest item; and apply 
timestamp-constrained versions of both shuffles. Five seeded draws are averaged 
within each user. Deletions compact survivors, changing content and positions 
together. Availability shuffles require complete monotone timestamps and 
approximate availability using training-first timestamps.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations
Results contain `metrics`—dataset, panel provenance/coverage, embedding 
alignment, intact statistics and conditions—and `metric_definitions`. Summaries 
include means, eligibility, missing-evidence reasons and conditional 
user-bootstrap intervals when at least 20 users qualify. Aggregation requires 
all four datasets and averages available category means equally; missing 
measurements yield null.

Position-only and position-preserving deletion controls are unsupported. These 
in-sample, two-candidate probes measure neither HR@10 nor full-catalog quality, 
causal preferences, simulator traits or checkpoint trajectories. The interpreter
prompt embeds measurements and definitions and requests a grounded JSON 
interpretation.

