INFO:self_evolverec:The new idea for diagnosis in iteration 3:
{
  "description": "Fuse each category’s frozen SASRec scores with a popularity-centered, Dirichlet-smoothed adjacent-transition residual. With training counts c_ab, source totals n_a, destination counts d_b, N transition occurrences and M real items, define q_b=(d_b+1)/(N+M), tau=10, and r(a,b)=(c_ab−n_a*q_b)/(n_a+tau). Normalize neural and residual components using frozen training-only statistics, then use s=(1−alpha)*z_neural+alpha*z_transition. Select one shared alpha from {0,.1,.25,.5,.75,1} using pinned four-category macro validation HR@10. Include popularity-only and occurrence-shuffled controls without using their outcomes for another selection round.",
  "motivation": "Electronics has weaker measured training-pair separation, and qualitative feedback suggests broad historical similarity sometimes misses recent purpose. Transition counts provide an inexpensive observable proxy for specific sequential connections. They cannot establish compatibility, immediate demand, or dislike, and no supplied validation evidence establishes improvement. At 10% research progress, a bounded correction experiment is more feasible than immediately training another model. FPMC and Fossil reduce the originality claim: the distinctive contribution is frozen-model correction with controlled mechanism analysis.",
  "implementation_notes": "Retain Movies_and_TV, Industrial_and_Scientific, Electronics, and CDs_and_Vinyl with separate models, counts and normalization, and unchanged routing. Keep DATA_DIR=os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], preprocessing seed 0, training seed 42, single-GPU execution and trial-local artifacts. Use the final configured baseline epoch checkpoint, default SASREC_EPOCHS=200, recording overrides; log any earlier checkpoint comparisons as search queries. Count only adjacent occurrences within original training histories, preserving repeats and excluding padding; do not bridge users or change splits. Build q with additive-one smoothing over real destination items and fix tau=10. For N=0 all source rows have zero residual. Empty histories and padding sources receive zero correction; after normalization explicitly keep their correction zero. Alpha=0 must bypass correction arithmetic and preserve SASRec ranking. For each category, deterministically sample 4,096 nonempty training prefixes uniformly with replacement from the original training histories and pair each with one uniformly sampled real item using a local seed-42 generator. Compute neural reference scores in evaluation mode through the same deployed feature and scoring path. Freeze per-component means and population standard deviations with a 1e-8 floor; save sampled prefix identifiers, candidates and statistics. If the reference residual has zero variance, disable its correction and record the condition. These reference samples estimate scale, not accuracy; their inclusive counts are acceptable for normalization and must not be presented as held-out diagnostic evidence. Do not tune temperature, tau, q smoothing or category weights. Evaluate six shared alpha values with the pinned validation protocol and select maximum macro HR@10, breaking exact ties toward smaller alpha. At the selected alpha evaluate a popularity-only residual −n_a*q_b/(n_a+tau) and three shuffled tables with seeds 43,44,45. Shuffle destination occurrences while holding source occurrences fixed within each category; do not shuffle unique edges or relabel items. Preserve self-transitions, destination priors, source totals, tau, and intact reference normalization across controls. Controls are diagnostic and cannot replace the selected intact model without a separately declared search. Store residual counts sparsely, with source totals and q enabling the dense popularity term without a dense transition matrix. Update the predictor writer to load the model checkpoint, item mapping, sparse counts, normalization, alpha, tau and dataset routing. Share exactly the same correction implementation with diagnostics and inference. For B×L probes, the source at each position is sequence[:, position], not the final item reused everywhere. Retain DiagnosisProbe(view, device), run_full_diagnosis(train_loader), diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis), the actual trained view.model, item_emb, log2feats and predict_score hooks. Return measured metrics and metric_definitions, with observation counts and unavailable results marked explicitly. Keep neural and deployed margins separate; inclusive deployed training margins contain transition self-count influence. For occurrence-excluded residual probes, decrement the evaluated occurrence from c_ab, n_a, d_b and N and recompute q and affected reference normalization without retraining SASRec; retain repeated occurrences of the same pair. Matched excluded nulls permute the remaining destination occurrences. Bound such probes by a declared deterministic sample and charge their computation to the budget. If the loader lacks sufficient occurrence provenance, report excluded diagnostics as unavailable rather than guessing the occurrence. Report validation target-pair coverage, unseen-source rate and support slices n_a=0, 1–4, and >=5, with counts, plus target-popularity and history-length slices defined from training only. Bootstrap matched per-user hit differences within each category and average categories equally; use 2,000 replicates with seed 42. Intervals condition on models and sampled candidates and do not correct adaptive winner selection. Keep full-catalog unseen recommendations for five real training users per category separate from sampled validation accuracy. Use only public histories, titles, descriptions and timestamps; review data, commercial metadata, simulator traits and hidden tests remain unavailable. No performance gains are asserted.",
  "pseudocode": "for category in four_categories:\n    model = final_configured_baseline_checkpoint(category)\n    freeze(model)\n    source_occurrences, destination_occurrences = adjacent_training_occurrences(category)\n    C, n, d, N = count_occurrences(source_occurrences, destination_occurrences)\n    q = (d + 1) / (N + number_of_real_items)\n    residual(a, b) = (C[a,b] - n[a]*q[b]) / (n[a] + 10)\n    reference = sample_training_prefix_candidate_pairs(count=4096, seed=42)\n    normalization = freeze_component_mean_and_population_std(reference, floor=1e-8)\n    save_trial_local_model_counts_mapping_reference_and_normalization()\nfor alpha in [0, .1, .25, .5, .75, 1]:\n    score = neural_score if alpha == 0 else normalized_fusion(alpha)\n    outcomes[alpha] = pinned_validation_all_four_categories(score)\nalpha_star = argmax_macro_HR10(outcomes, tie_break='smaller alpha')\nevaluate_popularity_only_control(alpha_star, intact_normalization=True)\nfor seed in [43, 44, 45]:\n    C_null = count(source_occurrences, permute(destination_occurrences, seed))\n    evaluate_null(alpha_star, C_null, unchanged_q_tau_and_normalization=True)\nreport_per_category_macro_support_slices_paired_bootstrap_and_null_spread()\nwrite_matching_predictor(alpha_star)\nrun_measured_compatible_diagnostics()\nlabel_inclusive_self_count_effects_and_report_occurrence_excluded_probes_if_available()",
  "originality": {
    "score": 3,
