INFO:self_evolverec:Research reports (2 report(s)):
INFO:self_evolverec:  Report 1: **Evidence and insights.** The starting recent-mean residual offers a cheap path for current interests. Its scalar gate cannot adapt to changes within a dataset. Electronics misranks 21.89% of sampled fitted pairs. Its recent-deletion HR@10 change is zero, motivating stronger discrimination and a direct recent-history path without establishing their cause. Movies loses 0.155 fitted HR@10 after recent deletion. Preserve its useful sequential encoder rather than replacing it globally.

Three literature insights guide extensions. [Negative-sampling research](https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.17276) shows that sampler choice changes accuracy and popularity behavior. Popularity sampling therefore needs controls. [MQSA-TED](https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.01056) combines temporal queries with transition information. This motivates asymmetric recent-item scoring, although transitions do not establish complementarity. [MoS](https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.20858) separates temporal interests. A small adaptive gate offers a cheaper hypothesis for this early, 10%-progress stage.

**Framework and candidates.** Organize methods along three axes: discrimination objective, directional representation, and temporal routing. SASRec supplies sequence modeling; the starting idea adds fixed temporal pooling; the selected extension makes that pooling directional and adaptive.

Scores are originality/potential/user alignment/model alignment/difficulty; higher difficulty means harder implementation.

| Idea | Scores | Positive assessment; negative assessment |
|---|---|---|
| A: Uniform 32-negative candidate CE | 2/7/4/8/3 | Simple discrimination control; current intent remains implicit. |
| B: Adaptive directional recent residual + A | 5/8/8/8/5 | Direct recent transition path; sparse transitions may generalize poorly. |
| C: Add randomly initialized title-token features to B | 5/7/8/6/7 | Shares evidence across sparse items; lexical similarity can repeat broad associations. |

**Selected: B.** Replace the scalar recent-mean residual with a gate conditioned on the current causal SASRec feature, recent summary, and prefix length. Average the last three nonpadding item embeddings, project this summary through a source matrix, and score candidates through a separate target matrix. Add this gated directional score to SASRec’s score.

This explicitly targets two observed user failures: stale history dominating immediate preferences, and broad similarity outranking a specific recent connection. Directionality models observed follow-on choices rather than symmetric resemblance; it cannot certify compatibility or prevent duplicate capability. Candidate CE targets Electronics’ weak fitted separation.

```python
h = sasrec(sequence)                    # causal features
r = causal_recent_mean(item_emb(sequence), window=3)
g = sigmoid(gate(concat(h, r, log1p(prefix_length))))
score = dot(h, item_emb(candidates)) + g * dot(source(r), target(candidates))
loss = cross_entropy(score, positive_index=0)  # positive + 32 uniform negatives
```

Exclude padding and known training positives from negatives. Use baseline, A, directional-residual-only, and B controls, retaining all four routes and prescribed seeds. Select exclusively by pinned macro validation HR@10 within the shared budget. Save both projections and gate; update the predictor writer and diagnostic scoring consistently. Preserve diagnostic interfaces and definitions, treating fitted probes separately from validation. No improvement is measured.
INFO:self_evolverec:  Report 2: **Evidence and insights.** The starting recent-mean residual supplies an inexpensive recent-interest path. A global scalar cannot adapt across contexts, but adaptive routing must outperform scalar controls. Electronics misranks 21.89% of fitted pairs; recent deletion changes fitted HR@10 by zero. This motivates discrimination experiments without identifying a popularity shortcut. Movies loses 0.155 fitted HR@10 after recent deletion, supporting preservation of its existing sequential encoder. Neither fitted margins nor embedding alignment establishes generalization or collapse.

Three literature insights refine the proposal. [Sampling research](https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.17276) motivates objective controls because sampling changes difficulty and popularity behavior. [FOSSIL](https://arxiv.org/abs/1609.09152), [SDM](https://arxiv.org/abs/1909.00385), and [MQSA-TED](https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.01056) establish precedents for transitions, temporal fusion, and transition-enhanced sequence modeling. [MoS](https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.20858) motivates contextual routing, although additional complexity needs evidence at 10% research progress.

**Framework and candidates.** Organize methods along three axes: discrimination objective, directional representation, and temporal routing. SASRec already models recent and older dependencies; the residual adds an order-insensitive recent summary and a directional candidate interaction.

Scores are originality/potential/user alignment/model alignment/difficulty; higher difficulty means harder implementation. Positive and negative assessments for every dimension appear in the implementation notes.

| Idea | Scores | Positive assessment; negative assessment |
|---|---|---|
| A: Uniform 32-negative candidate CE | 2/7/4/8/4 | Clean discrimination control; current intent remains implicit. |
| B: Adaptive directional recent residual + A | 3/7/7/8/6 | Explicit recent transition path; established components and sparse supervision limit claims. |
| C: Randomly initialized title-token features added to B | 4/7/8/6/7 | Shares content evidence across sparse items; lexical associations can reproduce broad similarity. |

**Selected: B.** Retain B as the eligible research hypothesis; implement A first as its necessary control. B targets two user failures: stale history dominating immediate preference, and broad associations outranking specific recent connections. Its asymmetric score learns follow-on associations, not compatibility, complementarity, or ownership needs. Candidate CE addresses Electronics’ weak fitted separation, without guaranteeing validation improvement.

```python
h = sasrec(sequence)
r = causal_recent_mean(item_emb(sequence), window=3)
g = sigmoid(gate(concat(h, r, log1p(prefix_length))))
score = dot(h, item_emb(candidates)) + g * dot(source(r), target(candidates))
loss = cross_entropy(score, positive_index=0)
```

Use 32 unique uniform negatives excluding complete training history, padding, and the target; specify loss scaling, initialization, and reproducible sampling below. Primary controls remain baseline, CE-only, residual-only, and combined. Further scalar-gate, capacity, and symmetry controls are conditional on budget; absent controls limit mechanism claims.

Prespecify checkpoints, stopping, and tie-breaking. Select solely by pinned macro validation HR@10; report paired within-category bootstrap macro differences if host user outcomes are available. Intervals exclude adaptive-selection bias ([Cawley–Talbot](https://www.jmlr.org/beta/papers/v11/cawley10a.html)). Preserve the sampled evaluator: sampled and full-catalog rankings can differ ([Krichene–Rendle](https://research.google/pubs/on-sampled-metrics-for-item-recommendation/)). Update predictor generation and diagnostic interfaces together. Report realized residual contributions rather than interpreting gate magnitude as reliance. No improvement is measured.
