Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)
The model implementation is not supplied. Diagnosis accesses the actual trained 
`view.model`, item embeddings, and architecture-compatible encoding/scoring 
hooks. `view.log2feats(sequence)` produces B × L × d features; the last position
provides the final sequence representation for recommendation probes. Encoder 
internals cannot be established from this file.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks
`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` receives training histories, optional metadata, 
and the model. Training batches contain `(None, sequence, positive, negative)` 
with B × L tensors. Scoring prefers `model.predict_score`, falling back to 
`view.predict_score`, and validates shapes and finite logits. Diagnosis 
temporarily enables evaluation mode, disables gradients, and restores module 
modes and process RNG states afterward.

# Probes & Metrics
- **Embedding geometry:** Samples up to 2,048 nonpadding item embeddings and 
computes `(mean pairwise cosine + 1)/2`. Around 0.5 means approximately 
orthogonal directions; higher values indicate alignment, without establishing 
recommendation quality.
- **Positive–negative separation:** Across at most ten batches, computes 
positive-minus-negative logits at valid positions. Reports mean, tenth 
percentile, negative-wins fraction, and fraction below 0.5. Larger margins and 
lower error fractions suggest better fitted separation; thresholds depend on 
logit scale.
- **Recent gate:** Reports the sigmoid of an exposed scalar `recent_gate`, 
otherwise null. This coefficient does not establish causal reliance.
- **Fitted reliance:** Measures ranking changes for up to 200 training users, 
using each final training event as target against 99 unique unseen negatives. 
Reports paired bootstrap intervals overall and by prefix length and target 
training popularity.

# Perturbation & Tests
Fixed candidates compare baseline histories with compacted deletions of recent, 
oldest, or random events, plus five shuffles of earlier events preserving the 
last event. Positive target-rank deltas, negative HR@10 deltas, and reduced 
top-ten overlap indicate sensitivity. Deletions also alter positions and 
adjacency, limiting attribution.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations
`run_full_diagnosis` returns `metrics` and `metric_definitions`, including 
sample counts, margin breakdowns, gate value, and nested reliance summaries. 
Missing measurements use null; category lists are empty. 
`diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` embeds measured results and definitions and 
requests grounded JSON interpretation.

These are fitted-model diagnostics, not held-out validation: probe targets 
participated in training. No four-dataset macro aggregation, position-preserving
removal, review analysis, or simulator-trait inference is implemented. Bootstrap
intervals exclude training-seed variation; persistent loader-worker RNG 
restoration requires caller support.

