ion unlikely to fit the remaining budget. Report skipped or incomplete configurations rather than treating them as comparable results. Select exclusively using the unchanged pinned macro validation HR@10; never access test data or change the evaluator. Log every attempted configuration and category-level validation outcome. If existing permitted validation outputs expose paired per-user hits, bootstrap 200 paired users independently within each category with CPU seed 42 and 10,000 replicates, average category differences equally, and report percentile intervals as exploratory uncertainty for fixed models and candidates. Do not modify the host evaluator to obtain these outputs. Retain DiagnosisProbe(view, device).run_full_diagnosis(train_loader) and diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis). Use view.model as the actual nn.Module; preserve item_emb, log2feats, predict_score, user_train, meta_data, and review_data compatibility. Restore the prior model mode in a finally block, keep measured metrics and definitions, mark missing evidence explicitly instead of returning misleading zeros, and leave unavailable-category breakdowns empty. Rank-based sensitivity diagnostics supplement existing raw margins; they do not replace the selection metric. Run bounded diagnostic comparisons in evaluation mode with identical targets/candidates and within the shared compute budget. Recent versus older deletion tests location sensitivity; shuffling within the recent window while preserving its membership and final item tests ordering beyond the order-invariant residual. These interventions may create distribution shift. Last-item-only, long-term pooling, additive pooling, lag weighting, window-length sweeps, deduplicated pooling, and shuffled-history retraining are follow-up controls, not additional configurations in this initial search. Repeated-history frequency can become a shortcut; deduplication controls can distinguish it from broader recent-interest effects. Unseen-item evalua