rving the latest readout item. It changes content, context and positions together. Identity uses unchanged inputs. No zero-item interior holes are introduced.", "Electronics:common_support": "older_substitution and common_* controls use identical successful user/draw/position tuples. Unprefixed permutation/deletion controls retain their broader original matched-suite eligibility; compare them descriptively. Means first average successful draws within users, then weight users equally; a user with one successful draw has the same user weight as one with five. Eligible IDs, attempted/supported draws and failed coverage are reported. Original seven-condition eligibility is unchanged.", "Electronics:optional_controls": "Temporal matching and explicit-position deletion controls are unavailable, rather than approximated. No architecture adapter, unchanged-input feature/score fidelity test, padding-key visibility verification or modified-masking baseline is supplied. Existing position-control nulls remain authoritative. Unchanged-history repetition checks float32 audit features and margins, not separate positive/negative score fidelity; it does not verify an explicit-position adapter.", "Electronics:prospective_pilot": "No reference fitting, validation-linked sensitivity or sensitivity\u2013deltaHR association is measured here. A future pilot must freeze baseline/last-item/additive-half-life-10 references, seed-42 shared fitting protocol, computation/query caps and comparisons before fitting; use the pinned validation users/candidates and host macro HR@10 selection. Log all comparisons and report common-support counts. Conditional user bootstrap intervals neither capture training-seed variation nor correct adaptive validation exposure. Native twenty-training-user full-catalog recommendations remain the host simulator's separate responsibility.", "Electronics:ordering_flip": "Fraction of user/draw pairs for which margin>0 changes truth value. Exact ties are nonpositive and reported separately.", "Electronics:feature_cosine_distance": "1-cosine between intact and perturbed final features; zero-norm pairs excluded. eligible_users reports metric-specific coverage.", "Electronics:deletion": "For n>=2 remove min(n-1,max(1,floor(0.25*n))) newest, oldest, or uniformly sampled positions. Compact survivors in order. Content, context, and absolute positions can change together; persisted deletion indices refer to retained-prefix positions.", "Electronics:shuffle": "Permute nonpadding IDs only, preserving multiplicities, targets and candidate IDs. Timestamp slots stay fixed. keep_latest excludes the newest slot from both swap roles.", "Electronics:availability_shuffle": "Window-restricted adaptation: minima computed over complete public training histories. Freeze all occurrences at their item's minimum timestamp, including ties. Scan unfrozen slots chronologically and uniformly choose feasible unfrozen partners j>=i with both swapped items available at destination times. Self-swaps allowed. Not a reproduction of complete-history author shuffling; training minima approximate availability, not release dates.", "Electronics:swap_statistics": "Displacement is fraction of original slots with changed item ID; repeated IDs can hide swaps. eligible_partner_mean averages feasible partner counts over attempted slots. nonself_swap_rate divides nonself swaps by attempted slots. No attempted slots gives null, not zero. Deletion displacement is undefined.", "Electronics:uncertainty": "1000 seed-42 user-cluster percentile bootstrap replicates of user-averaged measurements when >=20 eligible users. Conditional on fixed panel, candidates and fitted model; excludes training seed variation and search bias. No cross-checkpoint trajectory comparison or calibrated health threshold is claimed.", "Electronics:aggregation": "This result is per dataset. aggregate_diagnoses requires all four named datasets and computes equal-weight macro means only where all four provide a