INFO:self_evolverec:The new idea for model in iteration 4:
{
  "description": "Add a candidate-conditioned recent-history scoring residual to the unchanged category-specific SASRec backbone. For each candidate, attend over up to five causal input-item embeddings using both the candidate embedding and the existing SASRec state. Add the resulting candidate-specific score through a learned scalar initialized exactly to zero. Evaluate this architecture change with the baseline loss and negative sampler before testing objective changes. Candidate-conditioned pooling has direct precedent in DIN and DIEN; the proposed contribution is its bounded-window, baseline-preserving integration into SASRec, rather than a new attention mechanism.",
  "motivation": "The user diagnosis identifies unsupported broad associations and entertainment recommendations that miss specific mood or intensity distinctions. Candidate-conditioned matching tests whether each proposed item has support in particular recent actions, instead of relying exclusively on one shared pooled representation. These explicitly address two user-facing failures, but remain mechanism hypotheses: collaborative embeddings may not encode mood, intensity, purpose, or equipment requirements. The method does not establish compatibility, ownership, satisfied demand, or actual user intent. Quantitatively, sampled negatives beat positives in 17.4–24.0% of training pairs, with Industrial_and_Scientific weakest. The scoring residual targets candidate separation while retaining the stronger baseline sequence model. Last-item dot products and mean-history similarity perform poorly in the supplied training probes, favoring supplementation rather than replacement of SASRec. Prior residual scores below the supplied baseline make conservative controls essential; they do not establish that candidate conditioning will succeed.",
  "implementation_notes": "Architecture specification: for valid position t and candidate i, let h_t be the unchanged SASRec feature and e_i the raw shared candidate embedding. Collect raw shared input embeddings e_j from nonpadding positions max(0,t-4)..t, including the current input but never the next-item target. Set q_ti = W_h LN_h(h_t) + W_i LN_i(e_i), k_j = W_k LN_k(e_j), and attention logits q_ti dot k_j / sqrt(D) - (t-j). Position gaps are array-position gaps, not elapsed time. W_h, W_i, W_k, and W_v are distinct bias-free D-by-D projections initialized with Xavier uniform. LN_h, LN_i, LN_k, and LN_v are distinct feature-only affine LayerNorms with epsilon 1e-5, initial scale one and bias zero; reuse LN_i for candidate queries and branch scoring. Softmax normalizes exclusively over valid history slots, never candidates. Implement empty windows by producing zero weights without applying softmax to an entirely negative-infinity row. Compute m_ti = sum_j attention_tij * e_j and b_ti = dot(LN_i(e_i), LN_v(W_v m_ti)) / sqrt(D). Return dot(h_t,e_i) + tanh(a)*b_ti, where a is one learned scalar per dataset model initialized to exactly zero. Apply an explicit zero mask after branch normalization for empty contexts and padding positions. Do not normalize or otherwise modify the original SASRec score, and do not add branch dropout in the initial experiment. Initialize the new projections normally; zeroing both the scalar and projections could block learning. The normalized branch score is bounded in scale relative to an unconstrained dot-product baseline, so record its realized contribution rather than assuming comparable scales.\n\nInitialization and optimization: copy every matching backbone tensor from a canonical baseline initialization created with training seed 42. Initialize added modules with an isolated RNG without advancing baseline initialization, data-order, or sampling streams. Keep baseline BCE, optimizer, learning rate, regularization, batch size, data ordering, dropout configuration, and training negative sampler unchanged for the first comparison; log their resolved values. Do not silently introduce complete-history exclusions or different negative counts when the baseline uses another policy. Use unchanged nonpadding target reduction. Multiple-negative training is a separate future trial. At a=0, branch projection gradients are initially zero, but the scalar can generally receive a gradient and subsequently enable branch learning. Equality at initialization concerns deterministic eval scores for an identical baseline forward pass, not later training trajectories.\n\nComputational implementation: candidate attention adds O(B*K*5*D) interaction work at each selected position after projections. During training, score the baseline positive and negative candidates through the same function. During full-catalog inference for the twenty simulator users, chunk all eligible candidates without a prefilter so recommendations remain exact under the trained scorer. Candidate chunks reuse identical history context, with attention normalized over the five history slots. Catalog-wide LN_i(e_i) and W_i LN_i(e_i) may be cached only for fixed weights in eval mode. Per sequence and target position, cache W_h LN_h(h_t), history keys, raw history values, masks, and position gaps. Since W_v is linear and bias-free, sum_j attention_j * W_v(e_j) is algebraically equivalent to W_v(sum_j attention_j * e_j). LN_v must remain after aggregation; LayerNorm cannot move through the weighted sum. If a future variant adds projection biases, preserve them exactly and add the value-projection bias once after aggregation. Reassociation can introduce floating-point differences, so verify numerical tolerance and top-ranked item agreement, including near ties. Invalidate all caches after any weight update, checkpoint load, device change, or dtype change. Cache construction and full-catalog diagnostics count toward the search budget.\n\nExplicit context and diagnostic compatibility: define an immutable context object containing aligned history windows, masks, position gaps, target positions, source feature identity, and model/category identity. model.encode(sequence) returns baseline B-by-L-by-D features plus this context; model.score_candidates(features, items, context) is the sole implementation of total scoring. Selecting positions must slice features and context together. Final-position inference uses the actual final array position under baseline left padding, rather than assuming the last five array entries are all valid. Avoid mutable last-sequence caches entirely. Adapt internal diagnostic probes to call encode and score_candidates with explicit context. Retain view.log2feats(sequence) returning tensor features and callable view.predict_score(features, items); provide an optional explicit context argument for migrated probes. To support the original two-argument call on an unchanged returned feature tensor, bind its context by object identity in a weak-reference registry, verify identity, shape, device, and model/category ownership, and reject unknown tensors. Do not infer context from equal tensor values or the most recent call. Views or slices require an explicit context slice helper that registers the resulting tensor; do not silently accept unregistered slices. This compatibility machinery is a material source of difficulty and should be tested before training.\n\nPreserve supported B-by-L and B-by-L-by-K candidate layouts. view.model remains the actual trained nn.Module and view.item_emb remains its shared embedding. Preserve user_train, meta_data, review_data and the public loader tuple (None, sequence, positive, negative), with B-by-L tensors; unavailable review fields remain unused. Retain DiagnosisProbe(view, device), run_full_diagnosis(train_loader), and diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis), returning measured metrics and metric_definitions and constructing the interpretation prompt from both. Adapt all scoring probes to the complete candidate-conditioned score, including training margins, interventions, and full-catalog unseen-item recommendations for five real training users per category. Preserve diagnostic samples where possible, restore training/eval mode and RNG states, and include dataset identity in the view. Keep unsupported positional interventions explicitly unsupported. Embedding alignment near 0.5 is not evidence of collapse; training-target HR@10 is not official validation HR@10. Add measured scalar magnitude, residual/base score scale, history-attention entropy, and eligible sample counts as descriptive diagnostics, without claiming they measure intent or diversity.\n\nVerification before expensive runs: check zero-gate baseline parity, nonzero-gate checkpoint reload parity, causal-prefix invariance with identical retained position IDs, empty and partially padded histories, duplicate candidate IDs, batched users, interleaved contexts, position slicing, category mismatch rejection, and candidate chunks of size 1, 7, and the full candidate set. Compare cached and uncached scores using explicit rtol=1e-4 and atol=1e-5; log maximum error and any top-10 changes. Report failures rather than treating numerical tolerance as proof of ranking equality. Ensure target or future items never enter the history window. Save every projection, normalization parameter, scalar, window, baseline configuration, and mapping beneath the trial directory. Update the predictor writer so working/predict.py reconstructs the exact scorer and category routes. Use the same scoring implementation for training, prediction, and diagnostics.\n\nControlled experiments and alternatives: predeclare baseline first, proposed residual second, and a candidate-independent attention control third only if remaining budget permits. The third variant uses q_t = W_h LN_h(h_t) + W_i LN_i(e_t), preserving projections, parameters, window, branch head, initialization, and training while removing candidate dependence from evidence selection. Uniform pooling is a cheaper further control but does not match active parameter capacity. Shuffled candidate queries, softmax versus DIN-style unnormalized weights, zero versus nonzero scalar initialization, and frozen versus jointly trained backbones are optional subsequent controls, each changing one factor and registered separately. Shuffled queries require a fixed, logged permutation and are diagnostic controls rather than deployment methods. Do not automatically launch this full matrix. Consider the objective-only alternative if the residual fails; its stronger diagnosis alignment does not satisfy the requirement to address two user-facing failures as directly. Scratch TF-IDF remains a later avenue for distinctions absent from collaborative embeddings, with vocabulary and IDF fitted only on permitted training-available metadata and no pretrained encoder.\n\nEvaluation and reproducibility: retain DATA_DIR = os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], preprocessing seed 0, training seed 42, Movies_and_TV, Industrial_and_Scientific, Electronics, CDs_and_Vinyl, original splits, single-GPU execution per trial, and the environment's SASREC_EPOCHS default of 200. Record software versions, deterministic settings, baseline configuration, data fingerprints, checkpoint identities, and independent RNG states. Do not access unavailable ratings, review text, item categories, prices, stores, simulator traits, pretrained weights, extra datasets, or hidden test files. Titles, descriptions, and observed timestamps are permitted but unused by the selected initial branch.\n\nBefore execution, register validation every 20 completed epochs through the configured epoch limit, the ordered trial list, and deterministic selection: highest official four-category macro validation HR@10, earliest checkpoint on ties, then earlier registered trial on cross-trial ties. Evaluate each registered opportunity with all four categories through the unchanged host protocol: 200 users/category, 99 unique negative candidates, evaluation seed 42. Do not reconstruct or change the evaluator. Use matched checkpoint opportunities and optimizer-update exposure for controlled comparisons; separately report resource-limited outcomes when caps prevent matching. Freeze the selected predictor before independent final held-out inference. Log every attempted configuration and inspected checkpoint, including failures. Earlier supplied performance values are observations from prior variants, not controlled causal evidence.\n\nIf the authorized host exposes per-user binary hit@10 outcomes, retain paired user/category outcomes for identical candidate sets. Report category deltas, discordant wins/losses, and 10,000 seed-42 stratified paired-bootstrap replicates, resampling users within each category and averaging four equally weighted category differences. One extra hit changes category HR by 0.005 and macro HR by 0.00125. Users are the resampling units; negatives and checkpoints are not independent observations. Category-level exact McNemar tests or a predeclared paired macro randomization test are optional exploratory analyses; adjust any family of reported comparisons. Omit unavailable analyses if the host does not expose individual hits. Ordinary intervals and p-values remain conditional on trained models and fixed candidates, exclude training-seed and candidate-sampling variability, and do not correct adaptive checkpoint or variant selection. Fixed sampled candidates ensure repeatability but can reverse comparisons relative to full-catalog ranking; neither sampled validation nor twenty-user qualitative diagnostics establishes online quality or cross-domain generalization.\n\nBudget: the total shared allowance is 43,200 GPU-seconds, including all prior charged work, training, diagnostics, debugging, and failures. Read the host's remaining-budget ledger before scheduling; do not assume the original allowance remains. If no prior work were charged, an illustrative ceiling would allocate 12,000 seconds each to baseline and residual, 10,000 to the optional control, and 9,200 to integration, diagnostics, and failures. Reduce or omit optional work according to the actual remainder. Enforce allocations through host accounting, reserving enough to retain all four categories; wall-clock timers alone do not prove GPU-time compliance. Unused budget need not be spent. No execution, statistical significance, benchmark improvement, compatibility understanding, or held-out result is claimed in this report.",
