Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The module diagnoses a SASRec-compatible interface; model internals are not 
supplied. `view.model` is the trained module, while `view.item_emb`, 
`log2feats(sequence)`, and `predict_score(features, items)` expose embeddings, 
encoding, and scoring. Temporal probes require B × L × D features and use 
`features[:, -1, :]` as the final sequence representation.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` reads public training histories from 
`view.user_train`. The loader supplies `(None, sequence, positive, negative)` 
tensors. Histories are truncated and left-padded to `model.maxlen`. Diagnosis 
temporarily enables evaluation/inference mode, then restores module modes and 
Python, NumPy, and Torch RNG states. When available, `model.predict` must 
numerically match adapter baseline scores.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Embedding alignment:** Samples up to 2,048 nonpadding embeddings and reports
`(mean pairwise cosine + 1)/2`. Higher values indicate directional alignment, 
not necessarily collapse; there is no universal good threshold.
- **Training margins:** Across up to ten batches, measures 
positive-minus-negative logits at valid positions: mean, lower tenth percentile,
fraction below zero, and fraction below 0.5. Larger margins and fewer negative 
margins indicate stronger sampled training separation.
- **Temporal outcomes:** For up to 50 eligible users, predicts the final 
training event from its prefix against 99 unique negatives. Reports rank, 
reciprocal rank, HR@10, sampled top-10 overlap, and changed-minus-baseline 
differences. Repeats average within users; user bootstrap intervals quantify 
paired differences.
- **Descriptive controls:** Last-item dot product, normalized history 
similarity, and training-fitted transition scores provide comparisons. Five 
independently selected users receive full-catalog unseen-item recommendations 
per dataset.

# Perturbation & Tests

Tests remove matched amounts of oldest, recent, or random context; delete the 
final prefix item; shuffle earlier or all events; and substitute unseen items 
matched approximately by frequency decile. Deletions use packed sequences and, 
except final-item deletion, zero-filled holes. These reveal intervention 
sensitivity, but position changes and unverified padding behavior confound 
recency interpretations.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

Returns `metrics` and `metric_definitions`; a trial-local JSON additionally 
stores candidate pools, paired records, user descriptions, recommendations, and 
checkpoint identity. Metrics include strata, counts, omissions, scoring-contract
checks, and timing. Optional work has a soft 150-second allowance.

Official validation, four-dataset aggregation, and checkpoint associations 
remain unavailable. Training targets do not establish generalization. 
Categories, reviews, simulator traits, causal preferences, and verified 
position/mask controls are unavailable. `diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` embeds 
measured metrics and definitions into a constrained JSON interpretation prompt.

