  "implementation_notes": "Preserve DATA_DIR = os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], unchanged splits, preprocessing seed 0, training seed 42, independent models, and all four routes: Movies_and_TV, Industrial_and_Scientific, Electronics, CDs_and_Vinyl. Respect SASREC_EPOCHS with effective default 200. All artifacts belong beneath the trial directory. Keep execution single-GPU; all training, calibration, diagnostics, debugging and failures count toward the shared 43,200 GPU-second search budget. Reuse the same frozen SASRec checkpoints across fusion configurations; do not retrain identical neural models for each coefficient. Charge work according to host accounting and log both elapsed time and charged GPU seconds. No experiments are claimed here.\n\nFor each category, let N be the number of nonpadding catalog items. Count every adjacent ordered occurrence in training histories only: C[b,a] += 1, including repeated occurrences, and n[b] = sum_a C[b,a]. Never include validation or test interactions. Use tau=10 as a declared initial setting, not an established optimum: P(a|b)=(C[b,a]+tau/N)/(n[b]+tau). This is a restricted counting window W=1 with gamma_1=1. PCTM also considers longer forward windows with distance decay; reserve those for a separately declared extension rather than silently changing the reference.\n\nAt a query prefix, retain its last min(5,length) observed source items, newest first. Give occurrence j weight proportional to 0.5**j, normalized over retained occurrences; repeated IDs retain their occurrence weights. Aggregate log probabilities, t(a)=sum_j w_j log P(a|h_j), rather than log of an arithmetic probability mixture. Since log P(a|b)=log(tau/N)-log(n[b]+tau)+log1p(N*C[b,a]/tau), use T(a)=sum_j w_j log1p(N*C[h_j,a]/tau) for ranking. The omitted terms depend on the prefix but not the candidate, so this is exactly ranking-equivalent for fixed neural fusion. Unobserved pairs, unsupported rows and empty prefixes contribute zero. Preserve constants if actual